ubldr: pass the whole loaderdev string to disk_parsedev(), not p - 4.
p - 4 is the start of the string only for 4-letter types; for ide, mmc
and usb it is one byte before it, so loaderdev=mmc0p2 is rejected or not
depending on that byte.

Tutorial: FreeBSD/docs/ubldr_loaderdev_parsedev.md
Test: FreeBSD/docs/ubldr_loaderdev_parsedev_test.sh
Reported by: llm-postcr, POSTCR-d687c9fc7efe55d1ba7bc7bea056352ce0437588-1
Base: main at 29b24020f6fa (2026-11-12); needs d687c9fc7efe.

